# Code ownership → review routing. GitHub requests review from the owner automatically on any PR that
# touches a matching path. This is a small, single-maintainer project, so the default owner is the
# maintainer; the point of the specific rules below is to make the SAFETY-CRITICAL and CONTRACT paths
# impossible to change without that being visible in the review, not to distribute ownership.

# Default owner for everything.
*                                   @zgranowitz

# The cross-app contract. A change here ripples to the watch, Garmin, Mac, and widgets, and to the
# faBolusGarmin repo's Monkey C mirror — the schema-drift checks enforce the mirror, but the semantics
# are a human-review concern.
/schema/                            @zgranowitz

# Safety-critical core: the idempotency ledger, remote-command classification/validation, the send
# dispositions, and the transport gating. Dosing changes get extra review (CONTRIBUTING.md).
